{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>You stretched out Your right hand.</b> When the Holy One, blessed be He, stretches out His hand, the wicked perish and fall, for all is given in His hand and they fall at its stretching. And so it says: ״וַה׳ יַטֶּה יָדוֹ וְכָשַׁל עוֹזֵר וְנָפַל עָזֻר״ (Isaiah 31) — a parable to glass vessels held in a person's hand: he tilts his hand slightly and they fall and break (Mekhilta)." "<b>The earth swallowed them.</b> From here: they merited burial, as reward for having said ״YHWH is the righteous one״ (Mekhilta)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:27.319609787Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}